# Purchased source asset. Deliberately not committed: this repo is public, and
# publishing the .blend redistributes the asset rather than using it. The
# derived public/room.glb is committed so the site builds without it.
# Keep the original backed up outside git; see README for where to put it.
*.blend
*.blend1

# Audio, for the same reason as the .blend above and more so: the track in use
# is a commercial release, and this repo is public. Committing it would
# redistribute the recording rather than play it. The player reads
# /media/track.json at runtime and degrades to silence when it is absent, so the
# committed site still builds and runs for anyone who clones this. In the
# cluster /media is a volume; locally it is public/media/.
*.mp3

# The whole media directory, not just the audio: the cover art is extracted from
# the release's own ID3 tag and is exactly as rights-encumbered as the recording,
# and the manifest names a record that is not ours to publish.
public/media/

# Scratch space for files handed to an agent working on this repo, mostly
# screenshots of bugs. Tool-managed and local to whoever is working, so it is
# the same case as the capture directories below: generated input, not source.
.argus/

node_modules/
dist/
dist-server/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
tools/.venv/
tools/shots/
tools/preview/
tools/screens.json
tools/walls.json
*.local
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
